                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f2d17e39-3368-3c41-979c-c8479845af52",
                        "entry_id": "82bbc00b-a4e7-3f5a-90ba-afae65c5f1ac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "традиционное японское искусство складывания фигурок из бумаги"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "японск."
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "45d38f8c-34cf-4e80-8e9a-3567ea74ab38",
                                "sense_id": "f2d17e39-3368-3c41-979c-c8479845af52",
                                "text": "На сцене Музыкальной комедии было представлено древнее театральное искусство Кабуки, звучали потрясающие ритмы японских барабанщиков с острова Хоккайдо, проходили семинары по искусству икебаны и оригами."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b617acb-4c5d-4fe3-ac5f-82354a4576bf",
                                "sense_id": "f2d17e39-3368-3c41-979c-c8479845af52",
                                "text": "Собственно, все мы когда-нибудь да занимались оригами, вырывая листы из тетрадей на самолетики, лягушек и кораблики."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b321821c-d96f-393c-b8a4-d63c0513095f",
                        "entry_id": "82bbc00b-a4e7-3f5a-90ba-afae65c5f1ac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "изделие, созданное в технике оригами [1]"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "945714b0-bdbc-4a0b-a6cd-57e47c6f03b2",
                                "sense_id": "b321821c-d96f-393c-b8a4-d63c0513095f",
                                "text": "Из каждого листка, с начертанным на нём трехстишием, Шапиро мастерски, в один присест, складывает оригами и опускает бумажного журавля в обувную коробку, называемую отныне «птичьим базаром» или «птичником»."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "66c84c53-25aa-413e-b3ea-66a4ef3ca035",
                        "source_entry_id": "82bbc00b-a4e7-3f5a-90ba-afae65c5f1ac",
                        "target_lang_word": "origami",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "origami",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e0d0b22-53a4-3d18-80b0-515573bfff79",
                                        "entry_id": "c8fccea2-49ee-3df8-9262-7ca9badfdf56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The Japanese art of paper folding."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0961783-3075-4a86-9267-21160a9848b4",
                                                "sense_id": "2e0d0b22-53a4-3d18-80b0-515573bfff79",
                                                "text": "JongRak was a 10-year-old boy whose hands, eyes, and questions were all about origami: “Teacher, do you know how to fold a jumping frog?” With his deft little hands, he would teach me and the class how to fold a sunflower and a cicada. At some point, every kid’s little hands and pockets were filled with tiny origami models."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d6e84fd-3c4c-3e83-ab9a-c39e78872d0a",
                                        "entry_id": "c8fccea2-49ee-3df8-9262-7ca9badfdf56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A piece of art made by folding paper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41d471bc-6397-455a-99bb-95f62e7247e2",
                                                "sense_id": "7d6e84fd-3c4c-3e83-ab9a-c39e78872d0a",
                                                "text": "The production notes are folded like the funny origamis that I made in grammar school (only I used to write boy's names inside each section)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65f936f8-778d-305c-9552-9d9ced594386",
                                        "entry_id": "c8fccea2-49ee-3df8-9262-7ca9badfdf56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The materials science technology that applies the art of origami to products."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c78a3a87-3d27-3b5b-bb9b-e6ef52d6543c",
                                        "entry_id": "c8fccea2-49ee-3df8-9262-7ca9badfdf56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The materials science that studies origami applications in various material."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7225fca-25ae-3af3-ac9d-4afeaa175466",
                                        "entry_id": "c8fccea2-49ee-3df8-9262-7ca9badfdf56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The mathematics field that studies folding two-dimensional surfaces into three-dimensional structures, using folds and creases akin to those in the art of origami."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "origami",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb900534-8e6c-3972-bc4a-a8b85ad995c7",
                                        "entry_id": "cf0241a3-9c95-3d9d-a2a3-3bea4f7bd471",
                                        "glosses": [
